{"response":{"docs":[{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03315354","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03315354","description":["A shoot axis tuber of a potato plant (Solanum tuberosum)."],"label":"potato","obo_id":"FOODON:03315354","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03311532","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03311532","description":["Potatoes gratiné is one of the most common of gratins. Slices of boiled potato are put in a buttered fireproof dish, sprinkled with cheese and browned in the oven or under the grill (broiler).","SIREN DB annotation:\n* physical state, shape or form, multiple FOODON:03430108\n* root, tuber or bulb, without peel FOODON:03420240\n* water removal process FOODON:03460138\n* curing or aging process FOODON:03460253"],"label":"potatoes gratiné (dish)","obo_id":"FOODON:03311532","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["au gratin potatoes.","gratin potatoes","potato bake","potato gratin","potatoes au gratin","scalloped potatoes"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414704","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03414704","description":["Solanum ellipticum is known as potato bush and under the more ambiguous name of \"bush tomato\". Native to Australia, the potato bush is a small fruiting shrub in the *Solanaceae* family. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solanum_ellipticum]"],"label":"potato bush","obo_id":"FOODON:03414704","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415015","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03415015","description":["Apios americana, sometimes called the potato bean, hopniss, Indian potato, hodoimo, America-hodoimo, American groundnut, or groundnut (but not to be confused with other plants sometimes known by the name groundnut) is a perennial vine that bears edible beans and large edible tubers. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apios_americana]"],"label":"potatobean plant","obo_id":"FOODON:03415015","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["American potatobean"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03543894","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03543894","description":["The group includes any type of potato puree produced from boiled potatoes and often dairy ingredients, fat and salt, with possibly some flavouring ingredients. Here it is considered in the ready to eat form.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mashed_potato] and [https://www.google.co.uk/search?tbm\u003disch\u0026q\u003dPotato puree from potatoes]"],"label":"38940 - potato puree from potatoes (efsa foodex2)","obo_id":"FOODON:03543894","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03544037","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03544037","description":["The group includes any type of Potato crisps from potato slices. The part considered is by default the whole sold or prepared unit or a portion homogeneously representing the whole.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potato_chip] and [https://www.google.co.uk/search?tbm\u003disch\u0026q\u003dPotato crisps from potato slices]"],"label":"40370 - potato crisps from potato slices (efsa foodex2)","obo_id":"FOODON:03544037","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03307033","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03307033","description":["A raw potato certified by “Idaho® potato” and the “Grown in Idaho®” identifiers which are federally registered Certification Marks that belong to the Idaho Potato Commission (IPC). These Marks ensure that consumers are purchasing potatoes that have been grown in the state of Idaho.  The Certification mark pertains to over 25 potato varieties grown in Idaho, including the russet potato.","SIREN DB annotation:\n* whole, natural shape FOODON:03430150\n* not heat-treated FOODON:03440003\n* root, tuber or bulb, with peel FOODON:03420239"],"label":"idaho potato (raw)","obo_id":"FOODON:03307033","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411218","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03411218","description":["The potato is a starchy, tuberous crop from the perennial nightshade Solanum tuberosum. In many contexts, potato refers to the edible tuber, but it can also refer to the plant itself."],"narrow_synonyms":["Solanum tuberosum L."],"label":"potato plant","obo_id":"FOODON:03411218","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03306897","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03306897","description":["SIREN DB annotation:\n* whole, shape achieved by forming, thickness 0.3-1.5 cm. FOODON:03430140\n* fully heat-treated FOODON:03440014\n* starch FOODON:03420203\n* flavoring, spice or herb added, natural FOODON:03460229\n* food puffing process FOODON:03460268\n* ingredient: certified color added FOODON:03460133\n* ingredient: vegetable fat or oil added FOODON:03460263"],"label":"potato-flavored chip (puffed)","obo_id":"FOODON:03306897","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03307044","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03307044","description":["SIREN DB annotation:\n* divided or disintegrated FOODON:03430122\n* partially heat-treated FOODON:03440018\n* formulated mix FOODON:03530074\n* root, tuber or bulb, without peel FOODON:03420240\n* water removal process FOODON:03460138\n* food flaking process FOODON:03460274\n* preservation by dehydration or drying FOODON:03470116"],"label":"potato flakes (mashed potato, instant)","obo_id":"FOODON:03307044","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03309525","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03309525","description":["SIREN DB annotation:\n* finely ground FOODON:03430106\n* dry mix FOODON:03530090\n* water removal process FOODON:03460138\n* preservation by dehydration or drying FOODON:03470116\n* ingredient: flavoring, spice or herb added FOODON:03460227"],"label":"cream of potato-flavor soup mix","obo_id":"FOODON:03309525","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03316034","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03316034","description":["SIREN DB annotation:\n* root, tuber or bulb FOODON:03420238"],"label":"snack (potato-based)","obo_id":"FOODON:03316034","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03316134","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03316134","description":["SIREN DB annotation:\n* whole, shape achieved by forming FOODON:03430147\n* fully heat-treated FOODON:03440014\n* ingredient: grain added FOODON:03460152"],"label":"cereal and potato-based snack food","obo_id":"FOODON:03316134","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03316366","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03316366","description":["SIREN DB annotation:\n* solid FOODON:03430151\n* root, tuber or bulb, without peel FOODON:03420240\n* water removal process FOODON:03460138\n* preservation by dehydration or drying FOODON:03470116"],"label":"potato product (dehydrated, made from cooked potatoes)","obo_id":"FOODON:03316366","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411106","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03411106","description":["The sweet potato (*Ipomoea batatas*) is a dicotyledonous plant that belongs to the bindweed or morning glory family, *Convolvulaceae*. Its large, starchy, sweet-tasting, tuberous roots are a root vegetable. The young leaves and shoots are sometimes eaten as greens. The sweet potato is only distantly related to the potato (*Solanum tuberosum*) and does not belong to the nightshade family, *Solanaceae*, but both families belong to the same taxonomic order, the Solanales.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_potato]"],"label":"sweet potato plant","obo_id":"FOODON:03411106","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["batate","sweet potato"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414734","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03414734","description":["Gastrodia sesamoides R.Br. Is a saprophyte in the Orchid family. Common names include Potato Orchid, Native Potato, Bell Orchid and Cinnamon Bells. The Potato Orchid is found in Australia and New Zealand. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gastrodia_sesamoides]"],"label":"potato orchid plant","obo_id":"FOODON:03414734","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03400829","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03400829","description":["In EFG, Potatoes were excluded distinguished from other vegetables because of their high starch content. Some examples of foods classified here would be new potato, main-crop potato, jerusalem artichoke, sweet potato, yam"],"label":"starchy root or potato (eurofir)","obo_id":"FOODON:03400829","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03544036","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03544036","description":["The group includes any type of Potato crisps (also known as chips in American English), made of thin slices of potatoes or potato-based doughs, included those in form of small sticks. The part consumed/analysed is by default the whole or a portion of it representing the observed heterogeneity. When relevant, information on the part consumed/analysed has to be reported with additional facet descriptors.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potato_chip] and [https://www.google.co.uk/search?tbm\u003disch\u0026q\u003dPotato crisps or sticks]"],"label":"40360 - potato crisps or sticks (efsa foodex2)","obo_id":"FOODON:03544036","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03544038","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03544038","description":["The group includes any type of Potato crisps from potato-based dough. The part considered is by default the whole sold or prepared unit or a portion homogeneously representing the whole.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potato_chip] and [https://www.google.co.uk/search?tbm\u003disch\u0026q\u003dcrisps shaped from ground potato dough]"],"label":"40380 - potato crisps from dough (efsa foodex2)","obo_id":"FOODON:03544038","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00002536","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_00002536","description":["A potato waffle is a potato-based savoury dish in a waffle shape."],"label":"potato waffle","obo_id":"FOODON:00002536","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00002796","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_00002796","description":["A potato substance is a whole potato transformed into some derivative food material. It doesn\u0027t include potato food products that are ready to consume or simply require thawing or reheating."],"label":"potato (whole or pieces)","obo_id":"FOODON:00002796","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00003558","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_00003558","description":["A shoot axis tuber of a potato plant cultivar having golden yellow flesh."],"label":"yellow potato","obo_id":"FOODON:00003558","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["yukon potato"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00003759","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_00003759","description":["A tuberous root tuber of a yellow sweet potato plant varietal."],"label":"yellow variety sweet potato","obo_id":"FOODON:00003759","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["yellow sweet potato"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00003760","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_00003760","description":["A tuberous root tuber of a red sweet potato plant varietal."],"label":"red variety sweet potato","obo_id":"FOODON:00003760","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["red sweet potato"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00005168","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_00005168","description":["A Yukon Gold potato that has been boiled."],"label":"Yukon Gold potato (boiled)","obo_id":"FOODON:00005168","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["boiled Yukon Gold potato"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00005170","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_00005170","description":["A Russet Nugget potato that has been boiled."],"label":"Russet Nugget potato (boiled)","obo_id":"FOODON:00005170","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["boiled Russet Nugget potato"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00005172","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_00005172","description":["A Purple Majesty potato that has been boiled."],"label":"Purple Majesty potato (boiled)","obo_id":"FOODON:00005172","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["boiled Purple Majesty potato"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00005174","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_00005174","description":["A Sangre-S10 potato that has been boiled."],"label":"Sangre-S10 potato (boiled)","obo_id":"FOODON:00005174","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["boiled Sangre-S10 potato"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03401806","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03401806","description":["Includes any product that can be described/observed as a fresh commercial variety of Potatoes of varieties (cultivars) grown from Solanum tuberosum L. and its hybrids, to be supplied fresh. \nEarly potatoes means potatoes harvested before they are complete","LanguaL curation note: Index geographical origin in facet R,  growing method (conventional, organic) in facet Z."],"label":"10006104 - potatoes (gs1 gpc)","obo_id":"FOODON:03401806","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03540957","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03540957","description":["The group includes Potatoes or similar tubers sharing the same pesticide MRL, as defined by EU pesticide regulation. ] and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potato] and [https://www.google.co.uk/search?tbm\u003disch\u0026q\u003dPotatoes and similar]"],"label":"09570 - potatoes and similar- (efsa foodex2)","obo_id":"FOODON:03540957","type":"class"}],"numFound":339,"start":0},"responseHeader":{"QTime":0,"status":0},"facet_counts":{"facet_fields":{"ontologyPreferredPrefix":["FOODON","339"],"isDefiningOntology":["true","326","false","13"],"ontologyId":["ncbitaxon","363","foodon","339","ictv","148","pso","139","snomed","81","tfo","66","mesh","64","slm","43","chebi","43","lifestylefactors","37","ecto","30","gaz","18","to","17","flopo","15","po","15","micro","14","medgen","12","ror","11","dron","10","efo","10","pride","9","agro","9","ncit","7","fobi","7","envo","6","mondo","3","maxo","3","enm","3","go","3","gallont","2","peco","2","rbo","2","cco","2","slso","2","doid","1","oba","1","vto","1","bto","1","ppo","1","bao","1","ordo","1","vo","1","tto","1","hp","1","cdno","1"],"ontologyIri":["http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/foodon.owl","339"],"isObsolete":["false","339","true","9"],"type":["class","339"]}}}